lisa-design:
- Option 1 with option 2 as fallback: golangci-lint v2.11.4 `config verify` has a hidden `--schema` flag that takes a local path or file:// URL (pkg/commands/config.go, config_verify.go; FileLoader registered). The step downloads the schema from raw.githubusercontent.com at tag v2.11.4 (curl --retry) and verifies offline; only if that fails does it run golangci-lint's own fetch of golangci-lint.run, retried 3x on "validate: compile schema: failing loading \"https://" only, then ::warning:: and pass.
- Schema file is jsonschema/golangci.next.jsonschema.json at the tag: same blob (38b3e77a) as golangci.jsonschema.json at the tag and as golangci.v2.11.jsonschema.json on main / served by golangci-lint.run; the binary itself uses <commit>/jsonschema/golangci.next.jsonschema.json for unreleased builds, and golangci-lint's pr-checks verify against it.
- Pinned by tag, not commit SHA, so TestGolangciVerifySetup can tie SCHEMA_URL to the action's `version` input: a version bump without a schema bump fails CI.
- The verify step runs AFTER the action (verify: false) because golangci-lint is only on PATH once the action installs it; `!cancelled() && outcome != skipped` so lint issues and config errors both report. Running the action twice (install-only) was rejected: double cache restore/save.
- Known limit: with both GitHub and golangci-lint.run unreachable an invalid config only warns (nothing to validate against); the lint still runs.
- Config path comes from a new `config` output of "Choose the lint arguments" (shared config only); the repo config is found by golangci-lint's own search, as the action did.
